troke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Dry Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">granulated sugar</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"2\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">confectioners’ (powdered) sugar</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"3\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">cornstarch</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"4\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">ground cinnamon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">optional</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"5\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pinch</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-6967-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6967\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing ingredients</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Resealable plastic bag or bowl with lid&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For coating the donuts</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-6967-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-6967-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6967\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6967-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a bowl, mix together granulated sugar, powdered sugar, cornstarch, cinnamon, and salt. Whisk until everything is evenly blended.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6967-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Warm your freshly fried or baked donuts slightly. This helps the sugar coating stick better.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6967-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Place the warm donuts in a large resealable plastic bag or a bowl with a lid.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6967-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Add the sugar mixture to the bag or bowl. Seal the bag or cover the bowl, then gently shake or toss until the donuts are fully coated.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6967-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Serve the coated donuts immediately for the best experience. If you have leftovers, store them in an airtight container for up to one day to keep them fresh.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-6967-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>0g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>0g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>38g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s everything you need to whip up the perfect <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doughnut\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">donut </a>sugar for your delightful treats!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Donut-Sugar.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for donut sugar displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-6965\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Donut-Sugar.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Donut-Sugar-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>granulated sugar</strong> – 1 cup</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>confectioners’ (powdered) sugar</strong> – 1/4 cup</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>cornstarch</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>ground cinnamon</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon (optional)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>salt</strong> – Pinch</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-donut-sugar\"><strong>How to Make Donut Sugar</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making donut sugar is a delightful process that adds a sweet touch to your treats. With a preparation time of just 10 minutes and no cooking time, you can whip up this sugary coating in no time. If you&#8217;re using freshly baked or fried donuts, allow a few extra minutes for them to cool slightly before coating.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Donut-Sugar-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Four-step process of making donut sugar, including mixing ingredients, warming donuts, preparing for coating, and coating donuts.\" class=\"wp-image-6966\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Donut-Sugar-Preparation.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Donut-Sugar-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Combine Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, mix together granulated sugar, powdered sugar, cornstarch, cinnamon, and salt. Whisk until everything is evenly blended.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Warm the Donuts</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Warm your freshly fried or baked donuts slightly. This helps the sugar coating stick better.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Prepare for Coating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the warm donuts in a large resealable plastic bag or a bowl with a lid.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Coat the Donuts</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the sugar mixture to the bag or bowl. Seal the bag or cover the bowl, then gently shake or toss until the donuts are fully coated.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Serve or Store</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve the coated donuts immediately for the best experience. If you have leftovers, store them in an airtight container for up to one day to keep them fresh.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Dessert</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>12 servings</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Immediately after coating</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-donut-sugar\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making donut sugar</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use superfine sugar for a smoother texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix in a pinch of cinnamon for a warm flavor boost.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Coat donuts while they&#8217;re still warm for better sugar adherence.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with flavored sugars, like vanilla or lemon zest.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-donut-sugar\"><strong>How to Serve this donut sugar</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Dust warm donuts with a generous sprinkle of donut sugar for a sweet finish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a cup of freshly brewed coffee or tea for a delightful afternoon treat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside a scoop of vanilla ice cream for an indulgent dessert.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a topping for pancakes or waffles for a fun breakfast twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix into yogurt or oatmeal for a sweet breakfast boost.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Incorporate into a milkshake for a unique flavor experience.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can easily prepare and store your donut sugar for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow donut sugar to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container to keep it fresh.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store at room temperature for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For longer storage, refrigerate for up to a week.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap donut sugar tightly in plastic wrap or foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator before using.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place donut sugar on a baking sheet.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat for about 5-10 minutes until warm.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy fresh, soft, and delicious donut sugar!</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is donut sugar?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Donut sugar is a sweet coating typically used on donuts, made from granulated sugar. It can also include flavorings like cinnamon or vanilla to enhance the taste. This sugary topping gives donuts their delightful sweetness and appealing texture, making them irresistible treats!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. How much sugar is in a donut?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The amount of sugar in a donut can vary widely depending on the type and size. On average, a standard glazed donut contains about 10-15 grams of sugar. Specialty donuts with fillings or toppings may have even more, so it&#8217;s always good to check the nutritional information if you&#8217;re watching your sugar intake!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Can a diabetic eat a donut?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While it&#8217;s best for diabetics to limit their sugar intake, enjoying a donut occasionally can be possible with careful planning. It&#8217;s important to consider the overall carbohydrate count and how it fits into your daily meal plan. Consulting with a healthcare provider or nutritionist can help determine the best approach for individual dietary needs.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How much sugar is in 1 Dunkin&#8217; glazed donut?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>A Dunkin&#8217; glazed donut contains approximately 12 grams of sugar. This amount can contribute significantly to your daily sugar intake, so it&#8217;s wise to enjoy it in moderation, especially if you&#8217;re mindful of your sugar consumption!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Donut sugar is a delightful treat that brings back sweet memories and creates new ones! Whip up this simple recipe and indulge in the warm, sugary goodness that will make your taste buds dance. Enjoy every bite, and remember, the joy of making these treats is just as rewarding as savoring them. Happy baking!</p>\n",
